Logging:
By default below commands redirects only successful outputs
$ ls -l > log.txt
1 for success
2 for error
$ ls -lrt 1> log.txt  ->log.txt stores the success command output
$ls -lrt 2> log.txt -> log.txt stores unsuccesfull output. Here its does not store anything as it’s a success command
$lss 2> log.txt  -> log.txt stores unsuccesfull output
$lsss 1> log.txt  -> log.txt stores the success command output. Here its does not store anything as it’s a unsuccessful command

If we want both success and unsuccess command logs then use &>>
$ls -lrt &> log.txt   -> it stores both success and unsuccess command output.
$ls -lrt &>> log.txt  -> to append the both success and unsuccess command.

Tee command:
tee command is to write logs to multiple destinations.
 tee command writes to sandard output (command line) and also multiple files (log files) 
$ tee -a file.log  -> displays on command line and also writes to file.log
$ &>> file.log -> writes to file.log only

